# Raw-shaped doc-IR of the NXP KW47's pin-mux table, Table 58 "KW47 Package pinout", from the KW47
# Product Family data sheet, Rev. 4 (18 December 2025), pages 58, 59, 60 and 65. The tables are the
# docling output for those pages, unedited; the pages' other tables and text are left out.
#
# It is a FIXTURE, not a corpus entry. The PDF and the full doc-IR stay outside this repo.
#
# One row per pin, every mux slot in one cell ("ALT0 - ADC0_B13 ALT1 - PTB3 ..."), and a second
# column of low-power functions labelled by supply domain ("VDD SYS - WUU0_P14"). The awkward
# cases it carries, all real:
#
#   - A PIN BROKEN OVER A PAGE. PTA1's slots end on page 59 at ALT2 and continue at the top of
#     page 60 in a row with no name and no designator.
#   - A FUNCTION NAME CONTAINING ITS OWN LABEL. PTD2's "LPTMR0_ALT3" is one function, which a
#     label pattern without word boundaries splits in two.
#   - ONE SLOT NAMING TWO SIGNALS, wrapped after the slash ("WUU0_P2/ RF_XTAL_OUT_ENABLE").
#   - A FOLDED HEADER. On page 65 the producer joined the previous pin's last three slots onto
#     the "Pinmux Assignment" header cell, so the column cannot be found and the table is gapped.
